  "analysis": "The download failed because /root/.cache is only a 100M tmpfs, but the albert-base-v2 repo totals ~331M across 12 files (including tf/flax/onnx variants). The remount to 2G was denied (no CAP_SYS_ADMIN). So I must use a cache directory on a real disk with more space, and ideally only download the files needed for offline use (pytorch/safetensors weights, config, tokenizer) rather than all 12 files.",
  "plan": "1. Check available disk space across filesystems to find a location with >400M free. 2. Set HF_HOME to that location. 3. Use snapshot_download with allow_patterns to fetch only the necessary files (config, tokenizer files, and the pytorch/safetensors weights) to minimize space and time. 4. Verify offline loading with both AutoModel and AutoTokenizer.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "df -h / /app /tmp /root 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

